{
  "version": "keel.permit.action_classification_derivation.test_vectors.v1",
  "ruleset": "../../semantics/permit/action_classification_derivation_v1.json",
  "classification_registry": "../../semantics/permit/value_movement_classification_v1.json",
  "classification_registry_digest": "sha256:c46b8bd165ef16c284621e5349b22e5621fe66c4a25a3c8b18c8d88e20de76d0",
  "canonicalization_profile": "keel.canonical_json.payload.v1",
  "given_model": "Each vector's `given` is the verifier's explicit immutable environment: trusted_registry_digests (the trust set; step 3 resolves only a digest in it), and optional store_corrupt_digests / store_malformed_digests to model a trusted digest whose bytes fail hash-verification (step 3) or registry validation (step 4). The canonical pinned registry digest resolves to the real valid registry.",
  "conformance": "Passing every vector is NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT. The ruleset decision_algorithm, profile/grammar definitions, and verification_inputs are the complete contract; this corpus is mandatory minimum evidence. reference_executor.py runs the algorithm against every vector from the spec.",
  "step9_conflict_designed_out": "Round-3's step-9 counterexample (membership-absent + digest-false + observed yielding different outcomes) is not constructible in v1: integrity/digest checks are GLOBAL algorithm steps (3/4/6) before rule matching, and the rule's only per-rule predicates are membership and enforcement, both -> no_derivation. There is no valid/invalid precedence conflict inside step 8 by construction.",
  "outcomes": [
    "valid",
    "no_derivation",
    "invalid",
    "unverifiable"
  ],
  "deferred_coverage": "multiple-applicable-rules and rule-order-permutation need a synthetic 2-rule fixture (lands with the second Permit-to-X rule). Full canonicalization/Unicode/JSON-boundary suites and resolver-multiplicity are broader-assurance property tests, co-designed with the reference verifier. Named so their absence is explicit.",
